.TH SHARDPOSTCTL-ACL 1 "2026-09-20" "ShardPost 0.23.0" "ShardPost Manual"
.SH NAME
shardpostctl-acl \- read, explain and change mailbox permissions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shardpostctl acl list
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I account mailbox
.br
.B shardpostctl acl explain
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I account mailbox principal
.br
.B shardpostctl acl set
.RB [ \-mode
.IR replace | add | remove ]
.RB [ \-if-match
.IR etag ]
.I account mailbox identifier rights
.br
.B shardpostctl acl delete
.RB [ \-if-match
.IR etag ]
.I account mailbox identifier
.SH DESCRIPTION
Permissions follow RFC 4314. The owner of a mailbox always has every
right; the owner is therefore never listed as an entry. An
.I identifier
is another account of the user database, given in its canonical form, or
the literal
.BR anyone .
.PP
.I rights
is the usual letter string, for example
.I lr
(look and read),
.I lrs
(and keep the seen flag),
.I lrswipkxte
(nearly everything). The letters
.B c
and
.B d
expand to the newer letters, as in other servers.
.SS acl list
The explicit entries of a mailbox and the ACL generation counter. Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS acl explain
Answers "why does this person see (or not see) this mailbox?" for one
principal: the rights that apply, where they come from (an entry for the
account itself, an entry for
.BR anyone ,
or nothing), whether the grantee's registry holds the pointer that makes
the mailbox appear under
.IR "Other Users/" ,
and any findings in plain words. This is the command for share problems,
not
.BR "acl list" .
Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS acl set
Sets the rights of one identifier.
.B \-mode replace
(the default) makes the entry exactly
.IR rights ,
.B add
adds those letters to the existing entry and
.B remove
takes them away. The server computes and stores the change in one
versioned step, so two changes at the same time cannot lose each other.
The grantee's pointer follows automatically.
Role:
.BR provision .
.SS acl delete
Removes the entry of one identifier, which is the same as setting empty
rights. Role:
.BR provision .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-mode " replace|add|remove"
How
.B acl set
applies the rights. Default:
.BR replace .
.TP
.BI \-if-match " etag"
Apply the change only if the ACL is still the version you read. Both
.B acl list
and every change print the ETag. On mismatch the command fails with exit
code 65 and changes nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the answer as JSON.
.SH EXAMPLES
Rights on a public folder:
.B l
to see it,
.B r
to read,
.B i
to add messages with APPEND,
.B p
to let a Sieve script file mail into it,
.B e
to expunge,
.B a
to change its rights.
.PP
A public folder has no owner: without an entry, nobody sees it. Let
everyone read it and one team write:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl acl set '~public' Announcements anyone lr
shardpostctl acl set -mode add '~public' Announcements team@example.org lrswipkxte
.RE
.fi
.PP
Who has rights on a shared mailbox?
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl acl list user@example.org Shared
.RE
.fi
.PP
A colleague says the shared mailbox does not show up:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl acl explain user@example.org Shared colleague@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
Give a colleague read access, keeping whatever else is set:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl acl set -mode add user@example.org Shared \\
    colleague@example.org lr
.RE
.fi
.PP
Take away the right to delete messages, but keep the rest:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl acl set -mode remove user@example.org Shared \\
    colleague@example.org te
.RE
.fi
.PP
Withdraw a share completely, but only if nobody changed it meanwhile:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl acl list user@example.org Shared          # prints the etag
shardpostctl acl delete -if-match '"acl-7"' user@example.org Shared \\
    colleague@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
After changing ACLs in bulk, let the server check that every grantee's
pointer matches its entry; see
.BR shardpostctl-job (1):
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan acl_reconcile user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 65
The ACL changed meanwhile
.RI ( \-if-match ),
or the request conflicts with the current state.
.TP
.B 67
No such account or mailbox.
.TP
.B 77
The caller lacks the role, or the identifier is outside its account
scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shardpostctl (1),
.BR shardpostctl-account (1),
.BR shardpostctl-job (1),
.BR shardpostctl-mailbox (1)
